Making a paper (about 10 minutes)

Step 1. Exam Details

Fill in the exam type (e.g. Half Yearly Examination), subject, grade, maximum marks, date and time.
Click Next.

Step 2. Instructions

Skip this for now. The instructions are generated automatically after you add your questions. Click Next.

Step 3. Marking Scheme

Click Add Section for each part of the paper (A, B, C...).
For each section, choose the type (MCQ, short answer, long answer, case study), the number of questions, and the marks per question.
Check the banner at the top. It must show your planned total equals the Maximum Marks. If not, fix the numbers or use the balance button.
Click Next.

Step 4. Questions

Type each question.
For MCQs, fill in the four options.
Tick code block for Python code, so it prints in a bold code font.
Use the buttons to add sub-parts (a, b, c), an "OR" alternate question, an image or a table.
Do not leave any question empty. The paper will not generate.
Click Next.

Step 5. Review & Generate

Go back to Step 2 and click the auto-generate button for instructions. Read them and edit anything that doesn't fit your subject.
Return to Review and click Generate.
Wait 10 to 30 seconds, then download the Word file (to edit) or the PDF (to print).
Things to know
Don't refresh the page. Your work is not saved and you will lose everything.
Check the instructions line by line. The auto-text always says programming questions must be answered in Python. Delete that line for non-programming subjects.
Always open the PDF before printing. Check the page border, the logo, and that no question is cut off at a page break.
Don't change the school logo unless the admin asks you to. It changes for every teacher.
If Generate shows an error, the PDF converter is probably not installed on the server.
